der, wrapping\\\\ndocs/contracts.md:93:the bar can say `de otra banda sonora`. In `random` mode each scheduled\\\\ndocs/contracts.md:110:The `Mezclar bandas` toggle flips `mode`. Turning it off keeps the\\\\ndocs/contracts.md:201:The bar shows Play/Pause, Volume, a Cambiar track button (disabled when\\\\ndocs/contracts.md:202:Next has nothing to offer), a Mezclar bandas toggle with `aria-pressed`,\\\\ndocs/contracts.md:212:`de otra banda sonora`. On manifest failure the reader still renders and\\\\ndocs/contracts.md:227:The client sends ordinals and ids only, never text. \\\\\\\"Ilustrar\\\\ndocs/reviews/06.md:10:   Problem: the only pressed rule targets `button.chopin[aria-pressed=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\"]`. The `Mezclar bandas` button sets `aria-pressed` but gets no visual change, so sighted users cannot tell which mode is on. Screen readers hear the state; sighted users get nothing.\\\\ndocs/reviews/06.md:47:- No `requestSoundtrackChange`, `nextSoundtrack`, \\\\\\\"Cambiar banda sonora\\\\\\\", or \\\\\\\"Aleatoria\\\\\\\" anywhere. Copy is short Spanish sentence case with the exact `Just play Chopin`. Tokens only, Meta blue accent, no purple or gradients.\\\\ndocs/reviews/06.md:71:   Problem: the home becomes the best-coverage soundtrack, but the track is the best match across the whole style, so the bar can show `de otra banda sonora` right after a style change while the stored home names another soundtrack.\\\\ndocs/reviews/06.md:76:- Pressed rule: only the mix and Chopin buttons carry `aria-pressed` (`app/player-controls.tsx:39,49`); Play and Cambiar track are untouched. White `#ffffff` on `#0866ff` is about 4.8:1, past AA.\\\\ndocs/tasks/06-soundtracks.md:68:\\\\\\\"Cambiar track\\\\\\\" (existing Next): same-emotion tracks inside the current soundtrack in score order, wrapping, skipping current. If none, same emotion in other same-style soundtracks. Then best same-style overall excluding current. Null scene cycles the style set in id order.\\\\ndocs/tasks/06-soundtracks.md:113:The bar shows the soundtrack name next to title, emotion, composer or artist, license and link. When `isFallback` is true it adds a short quiet note, \\\\\\\"de otra banda sonora\\\\\\\".\\\\ndocs/tasks/06-soundtracks.md:115:New props on `Player`: `soundtrackName: string | null`, `isFallback: boolean`, `canChangeSoundtrack: boolean`, `onChangeSoundtrack: () => void`, `randomOn: boolean`, `onToggleRandom: () => void`. Buttons read \\\\\\\"Cambiar track\\\\\\\" (existing), \\\\\\\"Cambiar banda sonora\\\\\\\" (disabled when nothing qualifies), \\\\\\\"Aleatoria\\\\\\\" with `aria-pressed`. All copy in Spanish, short, sentence case. Real buttons with labels, visible focus, keyboard usable. Tokens only, Meta blue accent, never purple, no gradients, motion under 200 ms except audio fades.\\\\ndocs/tasks/06-soundtracks.md:146:- \\\\\\\"Cambiar banda sonora\\\\\\\" disabled state depends on the current scene emotion, so the reader must recompute it per scene, not once per manifest.\\\\ndocs/tasks/06-soundtracks.md:152:Martin simplified the UI to two controls, and this section overrides the design above where they differ. There is one `Cambiar track` button and one `Mezclar bandas` toggle (`aria-pressed`, off by default). There is no `Cambiar banda sonora` button, no `requestSoundtrackChange`, and no `nextSoundtrack`. The initial soundtrack is the one with the best emotion coverage, ties by lower id. Style is the user's choice through a selector, persisted with the session, and `requestStyleChange` moves the session to the best-coverage soundtrack of the new style without ever crossing styles.\\\\ndocs/tasks/06-soundtracks.md:158:Manifest v3 gains optional top-level `playlists`. A track gains optional `playlistOnly`, default false. Playlist tracks still carry `soundtrack`, `style`, and the required fields, but emotion selection never returns them: the filter lives in `candidatesFor`, not in each caller. Entering switches at once with `crossfadeSec` to the first entry. Scene changes stay tracked but never switch. Track end and `Cambiar track` advance in `trackIds` order with wrap. Exiting clears playlist state and picks the best match under the restored selection. The mode is never persisted. The button shows the playlist `label` verbatim, hides when the `just-play-chopin` playlist is missing or empty, and disables mix and style controls while on. The bar keeps title, credits, soundtrack, license, and attribution, and hides the emotion label and fallback note. The committed manifest has no playlist yet, so the button stays hidden until the Chopin files land.\\\\ndocs/tasks/07-picture-this.md:114:Selection flow: a `selectionchange` listener scoped to `main.book` shows a small floating button near the selection, labeled \\\\\\\"Ilustrar este pasaje\\\\\\\". On click the panel reads the live DOM once: the `p[id]` holding the earlier of anchor or focus in document order gives the start paragraph, and its `data-n` gives `n`. It imports the existing pure `pickActiveScene` for the scene button only and never edits `app/active-scene.ts`. Selections outside the book are ignored. Choice: read the DOM at click time instead of caching rects because cached rects go stale on scroll and each click needs one fresh read only.\\\\ndocs/tasks/07-picture-this.md:116:Scene flow: the companion panel holds a quiet \\\\\\\"Ilustrar escena\\\\\\\" button for the current scene id plus the image card. Card states: empty (no request yet), loading (\\\\\\\"Ilustrando…\\\\\\\" with a calm placeholder block, no spinner theatrics), ready (plain `img` with alt and caption plus a subtle \\\\\\\"Nueva\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\"Guardada\\\\\\\" note from the `cached` flag), error (friendly Spanish string only), and a small permanent note \\\\\\\"El chat llega más adelante.\\\\\\\" Polling: on `pending` the client reposts the same body every 3 s up to about 2 minutes, then shows a neutral retry message. Choice: repost instead of a status GET because one route keeps the lock, quota, and validation logic in a single place. Plain `img` over `next/image` because the CSP already allows Blob hosts and no optimization is needed. All controls are real buttons with aria labels and visible focus.\\\\ndocs/tasks/08-scene-reader.md:79:ArrowRight moves next, ArrowLeft moves prev. Keys are ignored with modifier keys and while focus sits in an input, select, textarea, or contenteditable element. Buttons read \\\\\\\"Anterior\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"Siguiente\\\\\\\" and disable at book start and end. On scene change focus moves to the text heading and the view scrolls to top. No announcement. Choice: silent focus keeps keyboard users oriented without noise.\\\\ndocs/tasks/08-scene-reader.md:83:Small quiet line above the text: \\\\\\\"Capitulo C, title. Escena k de n. Pagina i de m\\\\\\\", with the page part only when m is above 1. Choice: chapter titles are the table of contents, not spoilers.\\\\ndocs/tasks/08-scene-reader.md:91:Passage selection reads the current sub-page DOM as today and needs no logic change. \\\\\\\"Ilustrar escena\\\\\\\" takes the scene id from the route prop, and the `pickActiveScene` DOM scan in the panel goes away. Choice: the route already knows the scene, so scanning the DOM can only pick wrong.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"original_output_bytes\\\": 9695,\\n  \\\"original_output_tokens\\\": 2424,\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false\\n}\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18036-07cf-74d1-aaad-110ed763e167\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18035-a31e-73f3-8572-6907bca2a608\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18036-07cf-74d1-aaad-110ed763e167\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18036-07cf-74d1-aaad-110ed763e167\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/10-impl-aborted-a.jsonl:415:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c689\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18035-a187-7993-bea7-4a67b7092900\"},\"sequence\":415,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000825,\"record_type\"